export const FOREWORD = {
  id: "foreword",
  num: "0",
  title: { en: "On the First Cause Series", zh: "关于「第一推动」丛书" },
  sub:   { en: "Why a Chinese provincial press did, in 1992, what it should not have been able to do",  zh: "为何 1992 年的一家中国地方出版社，做成了它本不该做成的事" },
  body: {
    en: "The First Cause series — 第一推动 in Chinese, after Aristotle's Prime Mover — was the unlikely brainchild of a small group of editors at Hunan Science & Technology Press, a provincial publisher in Changsha. In 1992, when the first batch of titles appeared, China had nothing quite like it: serious popular science books, translated whole rather than abridged, with their footnotes kept in, sold for a few yuan in any general bookshop. The covers — deep night-sky backgrounds with a thin gold series mark — became instantly recognizable. The selection rule, never fully written down, was something like: would a great working scientist write a book for the public, and is the book honest enough to send to a beginner? Over three decades the series has run to more than a hundred volumes. It has been credited, in interview after interview with Chinese scientists born in the seventies and eighties, with being the door through which they first stepped into the actual practice of science. This site is not the series — it is one specific collection of thirteen of its volumes, organized into five subjects, and read as an atlas of what the series, at its best, has tried to do.",
    zh: "「第一推动」丛书——名出亚里士多德的「第一推动者」——是湖南科学技术出版社（长沙的一家地方出版社）几位编辑出乎意料的心血之作。1992 年第一批选题面世时，中国并没有什么像它的东西：严肃的科普译本，是整本翻译而非节选，附注一概保留，几块钱在普通书店便能买到。封面——深夜空底色加上一道纤细的丛书金边——很快变得过目难忘。选题的规则，从未被完整地写下，但大致是这样：一位活跃的伟大科学家会不会为公众写这本书？而这本书又是否诚实到可以送给一位初学者？三十年里，丛书已逾百种。在一波波出生于七八十年代的中国科学家的访谈里，这套书反复被提到：正是它们，是他们第一次踏进真正科学实践之门时所推开的那扇门。本站并不是这套丛书本身——而是它其中一处、由十三本书构成的特定合集，分为五个题目，并被读作「这套书在最佳状态下所欲为之事」的一份图集。",
  },
};

